"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HCHMQ59A1S0YB7C/prj_1HCHT9G2H1S05MYP/pjd_1KW8Z9MSA1S0Y1R0/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HCHMQ59A1S0YB7C/prj_1HCHT9G2H1S05MYP/pjd_1KW8Z98N01S0PR0P/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HCHMQ59A1S0YB7C/prj_1HCHT9G2H1S05MYP/pjd_1KW8Z7GBE1S0FE9C/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HCHMQ59A1S0YB7C/prj_1HCHT9G2H1S05MYP/pjd_1K6DEX8VK1S0Q7WW/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HCHMQ59A1S0YB7C/prj_1HCHT9G2H1S05MYP/pjd_1K5BKHZNX1S0GEN8/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nDAC\\n1,000Y+\\nDeep Sky Alpha\\nDeep Sky\\nISSUED\\n3.02\\nBUFFER POOL\\n0.061\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n02 Aug 2025 to 02 Aug 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nDeep Sky Alpha is a facility that evaluates the energy consumption, operability, and reliability of various direct air capture technologies under real-world conditions. The project encompasses the capture, liquefaction, transport, and sequestration of CO₂. CO₂ captured at Alpha is transported by road and sequestered off-site.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nCCTF\\nApproval date\\n30 Sep 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nDirect Air Capture v1.1\\nAccreditation\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nDeep Sky Alpha\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nDirect Air Capture (DAC) encompasses technologies that remove carbon dioxide directly from the atmosphere using chemical or electrochemical processes. Typically, in DAC, carbon dioxide in the air binds to either a solid sorbent or a liquid solvent, which then undergoes a regeneration process to release the carbon. The captured carbon dioxide can then be permanently stored using a range of techniques, including deep underground in geological formations.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n30 Sep 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 2.39 tCO₂e removed from Deep Sky Alpha on 11 May 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n2.395 t\\nSequestrations\\n9.943 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n7.499 tCO₂e\\n+\\nLosses\\n49 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n29 Jun 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n29 Jun 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Sep 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Sep 2025\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n08 Aug 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 5\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n3.02\\nRetired\\n1\\nBuffer pool\\n0.061\\nCrediting period\\n02 Aug 2025 to 02 Aug 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n28 Jun 2026\\t3.02\\t0.061\\t2.959\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Deep Sky's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.061 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.061 certificates.\\n\\nDeep Sky has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"